# Udev rules for ASUS Aura Sync Hardware on Linux
# Target: ASUS ROG Strix GeForce GTX 1060 & ROG STRIX Z270E GAMING

# 1. Allow group 'i2c' read/write access to NVIDIA GPU I2C character device
KERNEL=="i2c-[0-9]*", GROUP="i2c", MODE="0660"

# NOTE: this matches EVERY i2c bus, not just the GPU. Group members get raw access to all
# of them (including DIMM SPD buses). Add only users you trust to the 'i2c' group.
# The CLI itself only talks to /dev/i2c-0 address 0x29 and checks the GPU signature first.
#
# 2. The motherboard uses /dev/port, which udev rules cannot open up. Run those commands
#    through sudo; see "Safety and permissions" in README.md and SECURITY.md for a
#    least-privilege sudoers rule (it requires a root-owned binary, not one from target/).
